Demo script: the waveform authenticity line is now a never-cut beat

Added the delivery line for the hydrophone shot, with the camera direction to
point at the 15.9s spike while saying it:

  "This isn't an animation. It's the actual loudness of the actual ocean
   recording our agent listened to, and that spike is a real event at 15.9
   seconds into the clip."

Promoted to the never-cut list alongside the band ruler and the VERIFIED
badges: nearly every hackathon dashboard waveform is a random pulsing
animation, so the one sentence establishing this one is computed from the
committed audio file is the sharpest differentiator in the video.

Chain of custody, for anyone checking: NOAA public recording, fetched by
scripts/fetch_data.ps1, the exact 60s clip committed in the repo,
core/waveform.py computes the 320-bucket envelope, the page draws those
numbers. Tests assert the envelope matches a real 60s 16 kHz recording and
fail the build if Math.random ever appears on the page.
